  "body": "The maintainer asked for this in chat on 2026-11-17, with a screenshot of the title bar of Solidcraft (his own CAD program):\n\n> in solidcraft we have a home button that goes to a \"recent projects\" splash page, also version number is up there\n\nWanted:\n- A Home button in the top bar. It opens a start page that lists the recent projects.\n- A click on a recent project opens it. A project file that is not there any more shows as missing and gives no crash.\n- The start page shows when the program starts with no project.\n- The version number shows in the top bar, at the right, as in the reference (`v0.44.1` there).\n\nRules that apply:\n- The list of recent projects is application state, not document state. It is stored in the user's settings, not in a project file.\n- To open a project from the page uses the same command path as File > Open. A document with unsaved changes gets the usual question first.\n- `crates/ui/AGENTS.md` and the theme apply. The icons come from Tabler Icons. All text and icons are our own.\n- The page has a named layout test (`layout_page_<page>`) and a behaviour test.\n- MCP: if a command is added, it ships with its MCP tool, or a follow-up issue is filed.\n\nRelated: #1696 (the report dialog) and the Donate button issue are the other parts of the same request.\n\nDone means: the Home button, the recent projects page and the version label are in the top bar, with their tests, and before/after screenshots are in the PR body.\n",
